WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.000
Uniswap lets people swap digital assets directly from their own wallets. Official figures show more than four trillion US dollars in cumulative volume, used by millions of swappers.

2
00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:14.000
Trades follow public onchain rules. You do not need to give a centralized exchange custody of your assets before you begin.

3
00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:22.000
When someone swaps assets on Uniswap, the transaction pays a fee according to the public rules of that liquidity pool.

4
00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:30.000
People supply the digital assets that make swaps possible, and can receive a share of those fees under the pool rules.

5
00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:38.000
Participating on your own means understanding asset allocation and price ranges, monitoring continuously, and adjusting when markets move.

6
00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:48.000
UniEddy brings those complex tasks into one simpler flow. The system monitors continuously, AI provides analysis, and fixed rules decide whether to act.

7
00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:56.000
Fees come from real trades, and settlement and claim records can be checked onchain. Fee income is not guaranteed, and participating assets can rise or fall in value.

8
00:00:56.000 --> 00:01:00.000
Enter the DApp to explore how you can participate. If you need help, official guidance is also available.
